{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bs8jWAUaNLqPzSqjqLdX85","type":"tool_result","content":"                if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(this, name)) {\n                    const pre = (this as any)[name]\n                    delete (this as any)[name]\n                    ;(this as any)[name] = pre\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        connectedCallback () {\n            // Back before the queued teardown ran: this was a move.\n            if (this._live) return\n            this._live = true\n            // Start a fresh cleanup scope for each connection cycle.\n            this._cleanups = []\n\n            // Hydrate prop signals from attributes; preserve any\n            // programmatically-set value when the attribute is absent.\n            for (const [name, coercer] of Object.entries(propDefs)) {\n                const attrVal = this.getAttribute(name)\n                if (attrVal !== null && !this._bound[name]()) {\n                    (this._props[name] as Signal<unknown>)(coercer(attrVal))\n                }\n            }\n\n            const cleanups = this._cleanups\n            const props = this._props as PropsSignals<Props>\n\n            // Reactive Proxy: reading a key inside a ctx.effect creates\n            // a subscription to the provider's alien-signals signal.\n            const contexts = new Proxy({} as Record<string, unknown>, {\n                get: (_target, key) => {\n                    if (typeof key !== 'string') return undefined\n                    const token = ctxDefs[key]\n                    if (!token) return undefined\n                    const sig = resolveContextSignal(this, token)\n                    return sig ? sig() : undefined\n                },\n                has: (_target, key) => {\n                    if (typeof key !== 'string') return false\n                    return key in ctxDefs\n                },\n            })\n\n            let setupRan = false\n            // Tracks pending-context cancel functions so they are\n            // removed from the global registry when setup runs or\n            // when the element disconnects.\n            const cancelCallbacks:(() => void)[] = []\n\n            const tryRunSetup = ():void => {\n                if (setupRan) return\n                for (const token of Object.values(ctxDefs)) {\n                    if (!resolveContextSignal(this, token)) return\n                }\n                setupRan = true\n                for (const cancel of cancelCallbacks) cancel()\n                cancelCallbacks.length = 0\n\n                const refs = collectRefs(this, refDefs)\n                const ctx = makeSetupContext(\n                    this, props, refs, contexts, cleanups\n                )\n                setup(ctx)\n            }\n\n            // Deferred variant: skip if element was disconnected before\n            // the context became available.\n            const tryRunSetupIfConnected = ():void => {\n                if (!this.isConnected) return\n                tryRunSetup()\n            }\n\n            // Register pending listeners for any missing contexts.\n            for (const token of Object.values(ctxDefs)) {\n                if (!resolveContextSignal(this, token)) {\n                    const cancel = onContextAvailable(\ntransform adds it to any module where it keeps a `.render` link, so\nonly code that calls a `render` or `renderParts` static without\neither needs this import. See\n[ADR-009](./docs/adr/ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md).\n\n---\n\n### `microtags/preact`\n\nUse a microtags component inside a Preact app, rendered on the server\nand hydrated in the browser, or rendered client-only. `toPreact(El,\n{ events })` takes an element class and returns a Preact component that\nrenders the host tag. Preact owns the host and its attributes, and the\nelement owns the host's children. See\n[ADR-010](./docs/adr/ADR-010-preact-adapter-ownership-split.md).\n\n```ts\nimport { toPreact } from 'microtags/preact'\nimport { NumberInput } from './number-input.js'\n\n// callback prop name -> DOM event name\nexport const PreactNumberInput = toPreact(NumberInput, {\n    events: { onChange: 'number-input:change' },\n})\n```\n\nThe component takes the element's declared props (typed from the\nclass), one callback prop per entry in `events`, and `class`, `id`,\n`aria-*` and `data-*` props, which pass through to the host.\n\n**Server render, then hydrate.** On the server, the adapter fills the\nhost with the component's own markup, so `renderToString` gives the\nsame HTML as the component's `render` static. Server code must import\na variant of the component that keeps its `.render` link; a class with\nno render link throws an error naming its tag.\n\n```ts\n// server\nimport { h } from 'preact'\nimport { renderToString } from 'preact-render-to-string'\n\nconst body = renderToString(h(App, null))\n```\n\n```ts\n// browser\nimport { h, hydrate } from 'preact'\n\nhydrate(h(App, null), document.getElementById('root')!)\n```\n\nIn `App`, use the component like any other:\n\n```ts\nh(PreactNumberInput, {\n    min: 1,\n    class: 'qty',\n    onChange: (ev:CustomEvent) => setQty(ev.detail),\n})\n```\n\nIn the browser, the host gets a fixed, empty `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.\nWhile hydrating, Preact leaves that element's children alone, so the\nelement adopts the server markup. Because the value never changes,\nlater renders never write `innerHTML` either.\n\n**Client-only render.** With no server markup, call Preact's `render`.\nThe first render empties the host once, and the element renders itself\nwhen it connects, so the browser bundle needs the variant of the\ncomponent that keeps its render link.\n\n```ts\nimport { h, render } from 'preact'\n\nrender(h(PreactNumberInput, { min: 1 }), document.body)\n```\n\n**Two builds.** The import resolves by export condition, the same way\nas [`microtags/htm`](#microtagshtm). The `browser` condition selects a\nbuild that contains no render code. The default build, for Node and\nSSR, imports [`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support).\n\n**Peer dependency.** `preact` is an optional peer dependency. Install\nit yourself. Only `microtags/preact` imports it.\n\n**No children.** The adapter does not accept Preact children. Passing\nthem is a type error, and the adapter throws.\n\n**Props before definition.** If the element is not defined yet when\nPreact first sets a prop, the element has no property by that name, so\nPreact sets an attribute instead. The component reads its declared\nprops from attributes when it connects, so a value that survives\nconversion to an attribute string still arrives. The adapter does not work around this.\n\n**Other host renderers.** The adapter is built on the\n[`renderParts`](#builderrenderfn-options) static, which returns the","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5315d5cc-ff1b-47b5-b928-3130c18aca4f","uuid":"a7a6365f-6d47-456d-83b4-1f85f60720c4","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:24:27.447Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"                if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(this, name)) {\n                    const pre = (this as any)[name]\n                    delete (this as any)[name]\n                    ;(this as any)[name] = pre\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        connectedCallback () {\n            // Back before the queued teardown ran: this was a move.\n            if (this._live) return\n            this._live = true\n            // Start a fresh cleanup scope for each connection cycle.\n            this._cleanups = []\n\n            // Hydrate prop signals from attributes; preserve any\n            // programmatically-set value when the attribute is absent.\n            for (const [name, coercer] of Object.entries(propDefs)) {\n                const attrVal = this.getAttribute(name)\n                if (attrVal !== null && !this._bo