{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrspsS2Cek8t37gqGfMR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote three findings to `.nightralph/findings.md`, most severe first. Before that I built the branch and ran the Node suites: `test:ssr`, `test:preact-ssr` and `test:bundles` all pass, and every size-limit entry is under its limit. I did not run the browser suite.\n\n1. **Client-only Preact render leaves the host empty.** The README and ADR-010 say that on a client-only mount \"the element renders itself when it connects\". Core's `connectedCallback` (`src/factory.ts:133`) never renders into an empty host, and `AGENTS.md` says the same. For an ordinary component, `render(h(PC, props), div)` gives an empty host, and setup finds no refs. The client-only test in `test/preact-browser.ts` only passes because its fixture writes its own markup into `innerHTML` during setup, which no real component (such as `number-input`) does.\n\n2. **Preact never assigns declared props to the element during `hydrate`.** Preact 10.29.7 (`node_modules/preact/src/diff/index.js:531-536`) skips every prop that isn't a function while hydrating. It then stores those values as the old props, so a later render that passes the same object never assigns it either. A prop-only value, such as `items` passed as an array, is never in the server attributes. So after hydrate, the element keeps its default for good. No test covers this; the re-render test changes `count`, which hides it.\n\n3. **`renderHost` output changed.** The spec requires its output to stay byte-identical. Before, `render({ n: 1 }, { attrs: { n: '2' } })` emitted `n=\"1\" n=\"2\"`. Now `attrs[k] ??= v` (`src/render-support.ts:67`) keeps only the declared prop. That is probably the better behavior, but neither CHANGELOG nor ADR-009/ADR-010 mentions it.\n\nThe version is still 0.0.14, but the spec leaves the release to a human, so I didn't count that as a finding."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":409,"cache_read_input_tokens":83158,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":409},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5315d5cc-ff1b-47b5-b928-3130c18aca4f","uuid":"49c51e8c-9a18-45e8-9f2b-d47cecd4c89f","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:25:36.244Z","request_id":"req_011CgrspsBeLghcTb6wjmjB4"}
